mb|3C|mb|P|mb|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|lb|*bWhat should South bid here?^^4C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Although partner will sometimes have 6 clubs, you should assume they have 7. Then |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| says it is okay to bid 4@C with a 10-card fit. And given I have a weakish hand, 4@C seems reasonable. Note that even if partner only has AKxxxxx of clubs we have 8 tricks and we might even have a diamond ruff.|

